@@@!atrep

@@/ at-prosa: the long-form prose pack - parts and chapters
@@/ over koine sections, the deep section level, abstracts and
@@/ the toc directive, epigraphs, asides, the endnote families,
@@/ ordinals and index terms.
@@/ Part of the standard library; composes with koine and its
@@/ sibling packs.

@=== part
@==[(taxis)] lemma
grammata
==@
@"text part (highest structural division)"@
===@

@=== chapter
@===[(taxis)] lemma
grammata
===@
@"chapter; may appear without a parent part"@
===@

@=== subsubsubsection
@####[(taxis)] lemma
grammata
####@
@"subsubsubsection"@
@^(###)
===@

@=== ordinal
@. grammata .@
@"in-text ordinal display"@
@""
The grammata is a numeric ordinal (representative form:
Arabic decimal), an alphabetic ordinal (representative form:
uppercase ASCII Latin), or a period-separated hierarchical
compound of either. The typesetter renders the representative
form in any number system or alphabet. Distinct from taxis:
taxis positions a simmere in a sequence; the ordinal sim
displays an ordinal inside running text or a lemma, preserving
the no-text-insertion rule.
""@
===@

@=== abstract
@="
grammata
"=@
@"abstract; concludes the top matter"@
===@

@=== toc
@=#=(depth)
@"table of contents directive"@
@""
Monosim. The parameter is the maximum heading depth to
include, or "all". Placement directive only: the table itself
is generated by the typesetter.
""@
===@

@=== epigraph
@"/
grammata
/"@ [hypograph]
@"epigraph; the hypograph is the attribution"@
===@

@=== aside
@|
grammata
|@
@"aside definition; onymized on the episim, genos-refinable"@
===@

@=== chapter-endnote
@^^
grammata
^^@
@"chapter endnote definition; onymized on the episim"@
===@

@=== endnote
@^^^
grammata
^^^@
@"endnote definition; onymized on the episim"@
===@

@=== index
@% grammata %@
@"index entry, visible (TENTATIVE symbol)"@
@""
The grammata is the index path; sub-entries are separated by
right angle brackets, and the last segment is displayed.
""@
===@

@=== index-hidden
@%%(keyword)
@"index entry, hidden (TENTATIVE; multi-word keys hyphenated)"@
===@
